                        "review": "Starts off okay, but rapidly drops into a pit of dumb.\nThe voice acting is poor quality and poor audio quality with huge gaps between each line.\nThe music is incredibly repetitive.\nThe dialogue is stilted and artificial at best.\nThe story [such as there is] is completely nonsensical and basically relies on \"everyone lied to you\" as the big twist.\nThere's no challenge in the point and click aspect, 99% of it is either completely arbitrary or incredibly obvious.\nAnimations are meh.\nYou can't skip single dialogue lines so during the massive exposition sections at the end of the game you have to sit through long-winded explanations that cover stuff the game already explained, along with the massive gaps between each line.\n\nNot worth it for full price, possibly worth it if it was 75% off.",
